  "question": {
    "text": "On the treatment of the following compound with a strong acid, the most susceptible site for bond cleavage is:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1vYpa-ON1_pGfQpI9Jrz41w06CCIbxDMiIwKiPJdW04.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7bufi",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{O} 2-\\mathrm{C} 3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qNWkf",
      "text": "\nO5-C6\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "vu6Tn",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{C} 4-\\mathrm{O} 5$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OMCAA",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{C} 1-\\mathrm{O} 2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The lone pair of electrons on $\\mathrm{O} 2$ is involved in resonance with $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{C}$. Hence $\\mathrm{O} 2$ will not be protonated.\nThe lone pair of electrons on O5 is not involved in resonance with $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{C}$. Hence, O5 will be protonated. Chloride ion will then attack least substituted $\\mathrm{C}$ atom (C6)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/oi7P82eSUhNkD19WtmDvBhhQDGvScUfgJilNt1GIzAw.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/xjwevVrVt1h4w4K_hBIH46TlBhTRptRkxRpIKj573GY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
